# Kernel config fragment: the launcher's per-app cgroups (development record #319; docs/LINUX-DESIGN.md 3, 6, 7).
# The launcher moves itself into launcher/ of its unit's delegated cgroup v2 subtree, enables the memory and pids
# controllers for its children and starts each app with clone3(CLONE_INTO_CGROUP) into apps/<name>/ (memory.current
# in `status`, cgroup.kill for the stop). The base is allnoconfig: CGROUPS and MEMCG are also in memory.config (#348)
# and the root knob (#296) with the same values; CGROUP_PIDS is only here. clone3, pidfds, CLONE_INTO_CGROUP and
# cgroup.kill need nothing more. Merged after rk3128.config by scripts/linux-build.sh.
CONFIG_CGROUPS=y
CONFIG_MEMCG=y
CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
